{
  "title": "RLC step ringing",
  "group": "Electronics — analog",
  "description": "series RLC step response: ringing (Q≈5) vs critical damping — f0 = 1/2π√LC ≈ 50 MHz",
  "schematic": {
    "notes": [
      {
        "x": 40,
        "y": -113,
        "title": "RLC step ringing — what this testbench does",
        "lines": [
          "A 1 V step (VP) drives two series RLC branches that",
          "share L = 100 nH and C = 100 pF (f0 ~ 50 MHz).",
          "Branch 1 uses R1 = 6 ohm: under-damped, Q ~ 5, so",
          "probe ringing (across C1) overshoots and oscillates.",
          "Branch 2 uses R2 = 63.2 ohm = 2*sqrt(L/C): critically",
          "damped, so probe critical (across C2) rises with no",
          "overshoot. Probe vin is the shared step input.",
          "",
          "Set R1.R = 63.2 and re-run to watch the ringing branch",
          "settle cleanly like the critical one."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "instances": {
      "VP": {
        "type": "vpulse",
        "x": 40,
        "y": 180,
        "rot": 0,
        "settings": {
          "v1": 0.0,
          "v2": 1.0,
          "td": 1e-08,
          "tr": 2e-10,
          "tf": 2e-10,
          "pw": 0.001,
          "per": 0.002
        }
      },
      "GV": {
